.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that slash is load-bearing. Written as `data/` these
# rules match a directory of that name at ANY depth, so `data/` also matched src/rbp/data/
# and `results/` would match any nested results dir. git stopped tracking the rbp.data
# package, `gcloud builds submit` honours .gitignore, so the image was built without it and
# its own test step failed with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rbp.data'.
# /data/* not /data/ -- git cannot re-include anything inside a directory that is itself
# excluded, so `!/data/evidence/` below is silently ignored unless the exclusion names the
# CONTENTS. This is the same class as the `/results/` mistake below and cost ten minutes to
# spot, because `git status` simply shows nothing rather than complaining.
/data/*
# The published numbers and the evidence for them ARE the artifact, so they ship. `/results/`
# was ignored wholesale, which meant `git ls-files results` returned 0: a cloner saw no
# tables, no figures, and could not check one of the 696 golden assertions in a repo whose
# entire pitch is that verification is a stage.
#
# data/evidence/ is the per-example model scores: 3,496 tracked files, about 72 MB, having grown
# as the bias-aware and region-matched arms landed. It is under /data/, which is ignored, so it
# needs an explicit un-ignore. It is what makes every deep-model AUROC recomputable offline --
# recompute.py rebuilds 285 published AUROCs from it to 3.33e-16 across the 94-dataset
# three-arm panel, and fails at 0.4 on zeroed input. Without it the whole evidence base lives
# only in a GCS bucket whose billing credit expires 2026-11-18.
#
# The counts above were 1120 files and 35 MB, and the claim was "95/95 datasets reproduce". Both
# were true when typed. The panel is 94 datasets with a 95th candidate excluded from three-arm
# results, so 95/95 was also the wrong denominator. An audit was right that this repository
# presents its comments as audit history, which makes a stale comment cost more here than it
# would elsewhere.
/results/*
# THE ROOT LICENCE PROMISES THIS FILE AND THE ARCHIVE DID NOT CONTAIN IT. `/results/*`
# excluded it, so `git archive` shipped a CC-BY-4.0 directory carrying no licence while
# LICENSE said both results/ and data/evidence/ carry their own, specifically so either
# stays licensed when extracted alone. data/evidence/LICENSE was committed; this was not.
!/results/LICENSE
!/results/tables/
!/results/figures/
!/data/evidence/
/logs/
# EXTERNAL AUDIT REPORTS ARE WORKING NOTES AND DO NOT SHIP. One was dropped into this directory
# while a session was running and `git add -A` swept it into a public commit. The repository
# deliberately keeps the development record on the `working-notes` branch; an auditor's report
# is not release material and is not the author's to publish either. Keep them beside the repo,
# not in it.
audit*.md
*audit*.md
/.preflight-ok
/.preflight-modal-ok
cloud/terraform/.terraform/
cloud/terraform/terraform.tfstate*
cloud/terraform/terraform.tfvars
cloud/terraform/tfplan*
cloud/jobs/rendered/

# LaTeX build artefacts. paper.pdf IS tracked, because it is the deliverable a reader wants
# without installing TeX; the intermediates are regenerated by manuscript/build.sh.
manuscript/*.aux
manuscript/*.log
manuscript/*.out
manuscript/*.bbl
manuscript/*.blg
manuscript/*.synctex.gz

# Build artefacts that were tracked by accident
*.egg-info/
cloud/terraform/.killswitch.zip
.DS_Store
